+
+## 3. Mapping verdicts: what alignment buys, what's genuinely missing
+
+**Already ACS-shaped (rename, don't rebuild):** the intake contract is a declarative policy set with three-way verdicts; the claim plane is an allow/deny decision point with TTL semantics; the stamp plane already speaks landed/rejected/admin-review — a rename away from allow/deny/modify. Naming these surfaces in ACS vocabulary would (a) make the existing enforcement points legible to outsiders and to future agents reading the SSOT, (b) let the #1787 lease-wiring and #2119 gate work cite a standard instead of ad-hoc contracts, (c) future-proof the tower if ACS reaches platform-SDK maturity (v0.1.0 churn is the counter-risk — adopt the *vocabulary*, not the wire, until v1.x).
+
+**Gap 1 — pre-action intercept is the real one.** Every SupremeAI enforcement point above evaluates **submissions and claims** (intake, claim, gate). The in-repo equivalent of ACS's inline hook — intercepting an agent's *next tool call* before it fires — does not exist; the watchdogs are all post-hoc (they detect, file, and stamp, never intercept). ACS's Instrument spec is precisely the missing pre-action layer, and the ARW plane (#2557) shows SupremeAI already *designed* a Guardian-style runtime and left it dark. **The dossier's concrete recommendation: when the operator executes #2562's ordered remedy (deploy backend route → set env → redeploy), shape the ARW revival as an ACS-Instrument-shaped pilot — hook taxonomy + verdict object — rather than a bespoke protocol.** That converts a dark plane into a standards-aligned one at zero extra design cost.
+
+**Gap 2 — live AgBOM.** ECOSYSTEM_MAP and the radar index are static inventories with manual freshness contracts (passes 25–29 exist because rows go stale). ACS's AgBOM inverts this: inventory updated *by the act of observing*. Full adoption is overkill for a fleet this size; the tractable slice is deriving the tower's 151-tool surface + federation repo roster into a generated AgBOM artifact with the radar guard's freshness discipline — a small, falsifiable CI gate, and a candidate future scout/bridge lane (not filed here; this evaluation is the deliverable).
+
+**Trace:** the repo's receipt culture (every landing carries a receipt WO with git-anchored evidence) already satisfies the *intent* of ACS-Trace; adopting OTel span conventions would buy machine-correlatable traces across the tower + federation, useful the day the #2538 verdict-plane cadence problem is fixed and cross-plane joins need automation. Deferred: no current consumer.
+
+## 4. Rejected alternatives (honesty)
+
+(a) **Adopt the wire now** (implement Instrument hooks in mcp-control-plane against v0.1.0) — rejected: v0.1.0 churn risk on a control-plane surface where fail-loud migration has already bitten twice (R66/R67 rename waves); vocabulary-alignment is reversible, wire-commitment is not. (b) **Write our own standard instead** — rejected: the repo's control contracts are already ACS-shaped by convergence; forking the vocabulary forfeits interoperability for zero gained expressiveness. (c) **Treat this as an ARW-unblocking ticket** — rejected: #2557/#2562 own that chain and its remedy is operator-ordered; this document only recommends the *shape* of the revival. (d) **File the AgBOM CI gate now** — rejected: scope discipline (#1739 asks for an evaluation; the gate needs its own falsifiable design round and its own radar row if adopted).
+
+## 5. Limitations
+
+ACS facts are grounded in the live site + repo README/specification tree fetched this cycle (2026-10-29); the nineteen-hook enumeration and example payloads come from the repo's README/spec pages and were not validated against a running reference implementation. SupremeAI-side facts are read from the local tree at 15e31d3 and live tower probes this cycle (work_claim verdict, intake contract fields). The verdict `adopt` is scoped to **vocabulary alignment + ARW-revival shaping**; machinery adoption (wire, OPA/Cedar dependency, AgBOM generation) is explicitly out of scope and re-decidable at ACS v1.x.
+
